    "title": "Hispanic Community Primarily Received News From Univision, Voted Conservative: Hispanic Business Council CEO",
    "text": "Javier Palomarez, CEO of the U.S. Hispanic Business Council, discussed with NTD's Steve Lance the effect of the government shutdown on America's small businesses. Palomarez also spoke on the implications of the approaching formal review of the United States-Mexico-Canada Agreement (USMCA) in July 2026 and YouTube TV's decision to remove Univision from its base plan.\nHispanic Community Primarily Received News From Univision, Voted Conservative: Hispanic Business Council CEO\nCEO Javier Palomarez discussed the government shutdown's effect on small businesses and YouTube removing Univision from its base plan.\nBy\n|\nPublished: 10/9/2025, 12:01:38 AM EDT",
